1
00:00:06,990 --> 00:00:08,240
Two friends race.

2
00:00:08,290 --> 00:00:09,930
One uses a calculator.

3
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:12,230
The other looks for shortcuts.

4
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:16,160
The first question is 4.7 times 9, plus 4.7.

5
00:00:16,210 --> 00:00:18,050
Can you find a shortcut?

6
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,490
Work out 4.7 times 9, plus 4.7.

7
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:24,010
Pause the video and try it.

8
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:28,520
4.7 times 9, plus 4.7 times 1, is 4.7 times 10.

9
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:29,580
That is 47.

10
00:00:29,630 --> 00:00:32,140
No calculator needed.

11
00:00:32,190 --> 00:00:34,710
Remember: you can multiply in any order.

12
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:37,640
And A times B plus C is A B plus A C.

13
00:00:37,690 --> 00:00:44,810
Reorder: 0.25 times 36 times 4 is 0.25 times 4, which is 1, times 36.

14
00:00:44,860 --> 00:00:45,990
So 36.

15
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:48,520
Take out a common factor, like 4.7.

16
00:00:48,570 --> 00:00:50,920
Change a decimal into a fraction.

17
00:00:50,970 --> 00:00:52,510
Or round, then adjust.

18
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:55,090
This is called compensating.

19
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:55,990
Your turn.

20
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:57,620
0.125 is 1 eighth.

21
00:00:57,670 --> 00:01:00,880
Use this to work out 0.125 times 64.

22
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:04,720
Pause the video and try it.

23
00:01:04,770 --> 00:01:07,430
1 eighth of 64 is 8.

24
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:10,170
Choose the method that fits the numbers.

25
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:14,960
If there is no shortcut, use a written method or a calculator.

26
00:01:15,010 --> 00:01:16,610
Here is the method.

27
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:21,170
Step 1: look for pairs that make 1, 10 or 100.

28
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:24,160
Step 2: look for a common factor.

29
00:01:24,210 --> 00:01:28,920
Step 3: change decimals to fractions, or round and adjust.

30
00:01:28,970 --> 00:01:31,850
Step 4: check with an estimate.

31
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:34,020
Work out 19.8 times 5.

32
00:01:34,070 --> 00:01:35,790
20 times 5 is 100.

33
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:39,630
Then take away 0.2 times 5, which is 1.

34
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:41,860
The answer is 99.

35
00:01:41,910 --> 00:01:42,690
Your turn.

36
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:44,520
Work out 3.99 times 6.

37
00:01:44,570 --> 00:01:47,740
Pause and work it out.

38
00:01:47,790 --> 00:01:49,440
4 times 6 is 24.

39
00:01:49,490 --> 00:01:53,450
Take away 0.01 times 6, which is 0.06.

40
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:56,120
The answer is 23.94.

41
00:01:56,170 --> 00:02:00,890
0.75 times 2.8 is 3 quarters of 2.8, which is 2.1.

42
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:08,790
And 3 fifths times 17, plus 3 fifths times 3, is 3 fifths of 20, which is 12.

43
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:12,590
Owen works out 6 times 2.5, plus 4 times 2.5.

44
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:14,820
Which line is wrong?

45
00:02:14,870 --> 00:02:16,020
Line 1 is wrong.

46
00:02:16,070 --> 00:02:20,400
Take out the common factor 2.5, and add the others.

47
00:02:20,450 --> 00:02:22,260
6 plus 4 is 10.

48
00:02:22,310 --> 00:02:25,170
10 times 2.5 is 25.

49
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:28,580
Shoppers use compensation all the time.

50
00:02:28,630 --> 00:02:34,990
3 items at 4.99 dollars is 3 times 5, minus 3 cents: 14.97 dollars.

51
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:36,390
One last question.

52
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:38,110
Work out 0.5 times 88.

53
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:41,620
Pause the video and answer.

54
00:02:41,670 --> 00:02:43,000
0.5 is a half.

55
00:02:43,050 --> 00:02:45,230
Half of 88 is 44.

56
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:48,530
To remember: reorder to make easy pairs.

57
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:51,020
Take out a common factor.

58
00:02:51,070 --> 00:02:56,660
Use fractions for decimals like 0.25, 0.5 and 0.125.

59
00:02:56,710 --> 00:02:59,040
Round, then adjust.

60
00:02:59,090 --> 00:03:04,230
Great work! Now practise lesson 8.5 on Camday.
